          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Is Dental Fluorosis?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            In several parts of Rajasthan, high fluoride levels in groundwater during early childhood can cause dental fluorosis—leaving white chalky streaks, yellow bands, or brown patches permanently inside tooth enamel. Other stains come from daily tea, coffee, spices, tobacco, or past tooth injuries. Because these marks sit inside or firmly on enamel, home remedies or lemon-salt scrubs cannot fix them safely and often scratch the teeth.
          </p>
