            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden"><button type="button" class="faq-trigger w-full min-h-[52px] px-5 py-3.5 text-left flex justify-between items-center font-semibold" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fl-f3"><span>Does composite bonding hurt?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 text-[#C1121F]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg></button><div id="fl-f3" class="hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">Usually no injection is required because composite bonding works gently on the outer enamel surface.</div></div>
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden"><button type="button" class="faq-trigger w-full min-h-[52px] px-5 py-3.5 text-left flex justify-between items-center font-semibold" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fl-f4"><span>Can paan or tea stains be cleaned?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 text-[#C1121F]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg></button><div id="fl-f4" class="hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">Yes, external food and tobacco stains are generally cleared through ultrasonic scaling and polishing.</div></div>
